---
import { educationalAbliteratedRows, testedAbliteratedStatus } from '../lib/ask';
import { abliteratedGuide } from '../lib/status';

const rows = educationalAbliteratedRows();
const status = testedAbliteratedStatus();
---

<aside data-abliterated-panel hidden class="mt-6 rounded-2xl border border-line bg-canvas/70 p-4">
  <p class="kicker">Abliterated / uncensored</p>
  <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
    Abliteration edits refusals in the weights. It can hurt quality. Verify the source and the uploader.
    You are responsible for what you run. Q1/Q2 stay off; Q3 is estimate/community unless measured. Read the
    <a class="underline decoration-accent/40 underline-offset-2" href="/abliterated">abliterated hub</a>.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-3 rounded-xl border border-warn/40 bg-warn/10 px-3 py-2 text-sm text-warn">
    Tested on our rig: {status}. Do not invent a daily-driver swap.
  </p>
  <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3">
    {rows.map((row) => (
      <li class="rounded-xl border border-line p-3 text-sm">
        <p class="font-medium">{row.name}</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-faint">{row.repo}</p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-muted">{row.method}. {row.quant_example}. {row.vram_32gb}</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-faint">{row.reliability} · llama.cpp first. {row.notes}</p>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>
  <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-faint">
    Catalog as of {abliteratedGuide.as_of}. Fit notes are the catalog’s 32 GB column, not a new calculator run — we do not invent KV math for these files. Q3 and up; Q3 is estimate/community unless measured. Confirm the live model card.
  </p>
</aside>
